  "method": "One fresh arm64 macOS process per lane and case. One balanced warm-up pair and 16 measured paired rounds per case. Cases rotate; each lane occupies first position 8/16. Timed duration covers C replay call with actual production callback, enqueue and worker-side drain with per-event oracle. Each process creates eight independent engine epochs with 4096 callbacks each, avoiding quota saturation. Initial operation creation and retirement occur outside each timer. Zero bytes represents a TXT watch callback, 32 and 2048 represent a resolve with hostname, service name and TXT. No real Bonjour/OS service, native discovery delay, parsing a published peer, network or UI is measured. Concurrent host work uncontrolled. Per-process mean ns/callback and paired percent changes are summarized.",
